      "external_id": "C11-CHEM-CH10-10.10.2-RU",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xi/chemistry/c11-chem/ch10",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/chemistry/c11-chem/ch10/10.10.2",
      "title": "10.10.2 Electron par charge ka hisab (Roman Urdu)",
      "language": "roman_ur",
      "variant_of": "C11-CHEM-CH10-10.10.2",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 223,
          "pdf_to": 224,
          "note": "Roman Urdu explanation of topic 10.10.2 with Quick Check 10.5, printed pages 223-224."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Neeche ek namoona hisab (sample calculation) hai jis mein 34 min tak 0.20 A current guzara gaya."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{shuru mein anode ki mass} = 56.53\\ \\text{g}",
            "text_alt": "shuru mein anode ki mass = 56.53 g"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{aakhir mein anode ki mass} = 56.40\\ \\text{g}",
            "text_alt": "aakhir mein anode ki mass = 56.40 g"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{anode se hata copper} = 56.53 - 56.40 = 0.13\\ \\text{g}",
            "text_alt": "anode se hata copper = 56.53 − 56.40 = 0.13 g"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "Q = I \\times t = 0.20 \\times 34 \\times 60 = 408\\ \\text{C}",
            "text_alt": "Q = I × t = 0.20 × 34 × 60 = 408 C"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Yani 0.13 g copper ke liye 408 C laga."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{63.5 g (1 mole) copper ke liye} = \\frac{408}{0.13} \\times 63.5 = 199292\\ \\text{C}",
            "text_alt": "63.5 g (1 mole) copper ke liye = (408 / 0.13) × 63.5 = 199292 C"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Lekin electrolysis ki equation batati hai ke 1 mole copper ke liye 2 moles electrons chahiye:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{Cu^{2+}_{(aq)} + 2e^- -> Cu_{(s)}}",
            "text_alt": "Cu²⁺(aq) + 2e⁻ → Cu(s)"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{1 mole electrons ka charge} = \\frac{199292}{2} = 99646\\ \\text{C}",
            "text_alt": "1 mole electrons ka charge = 199292 / 2 = 99646 C"
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Kitab ki ghalti",
            "text": "Kitab ne likha hai ke 63.5 g copper ko (408 / 0.13) × 63.5 = 99646 C chahiye. Yeh hisab ghalat hai: (408 / 0.13) × 63.5 = 199292 C banta hai. Yeh 1 mole copper ka charge hai; 1 mole copper ko 2 moles electrons chahiye, is liye 1 mole electrons ka charge 199292 / 2 = 99646 C hai. Aage L ka jawab wahi rehta hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Agar ek electron ka charge 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C ho to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "L = \\frac{99646}{1.60 \\times 10^{-19}} = 6.2 \\times 10^{23}\\ \\text{mol}^{-1}",
            "text_alt": "L = 99646 / (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6.2 × 10²³ mol⁻¹"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Yeh asal (accurate) value 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ ke kaafi qareeb hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Quick Check 10.5"
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "a) Silver nitrate solution mein 0.18 A current theek 35 min guzre to cathode par kitni silver jamegi? (Ar Ag = 108; F = 96500 C mol⁻¹)",
            "explanation": "Q = 0.18 × 35 × 60 = 378 C. Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag, to 96500 C se 108 g. Mass = (378 / 96500) × 108 = 0.42 g."
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "b) Dilute sulfuric acid mein 1.04 A current 6.00 min guzarne se STP par 41.5 cm³ hydrogen bani. i) Kitne coulombs guzre? ii) 1 mole hydrogen gas ke liye kitne coulombs chahiye?",
            "explanation": "i) Q = 1.04 × 6.00 × 60 = 374 C. ii) 2H⁺ + 2e⁻ → H₂, to 1 mole H₂ ke liye 2F = 2 × 96500 = 193000 C. Tajurbe se: 41.5 / 22400 = 1.85 × 10⁻³ mol H₂, aur 374 / (1.85 × 10⁻³) ≈ 2.0 × 10⁵ C, jo 193000 C ke qareeb hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Mukhtasar khulasa"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "0.20 A × 34 min = 408 C ne anode se 0.13 g Cu hataya.",
              "1 mole Cu ke liye 199292 C, to 1 mole electrons ka charge 99646 C.",
              "L = 99646 / (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6.2 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ (asal 6.02 × 10²³)."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
